From 75325fdaa8c37988d43b3a22984cd627e77d2ee4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duncan0k <dev@ark0.si>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:14:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 74/77] test: add fuzz targets for SLHDSA128SVerify and
 OP_CHECKSLHDSA128S

- slhdsa128s_verify calls the verification wrapper with keys, messages,
  context strings and signatures of any length, or the valid fixture with
  a few bytes or lengths changed. It checks that a wrong length never
  reaches the library, which reads the start of the signature before it
  checks its length, and that nothing but the fixture itself verifies.
- p2mr_slhdsa128s runs an executed or unexecuted SLH-DSA leaf through
  VerifyScript with every combination of the flags around it, chunk and
  key sizes at each boundary and hash types around the valid ones, and
  compares the result with the rules written independently of the
  interpreter, in their order. The verification itself returns a result
  the fuzzer picks, so that both outcomes are reached. The same input
  through DeferringSignatureChecker must give the same result.
---
